<title>SOUTH KOREA: Daewoo Motor union workers to strike from 1 p.m..</title>
<headline>Daewoo Motor union workers to strike from 1 p.m..</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union workers at South Korea's Daewoo Motor Co, a unit of the Daewoo Group, will strike from 1.00 p.m. (0400 GMT) on Friday, a union spokesman said.  </p>
<p>&quot;They will lay down their tools this afternoon,&quot; said Jung Jong-seung, a Daewoo Group union spokesman.</p>
<p>He said out of 15 Daewoo Group unions, 10 voted to strike, affecting a total of 32,000 union workers.</p>
<p>Workers at the main shipyard of Daewoo Heavy Industries Co went on strike from 8.00 a.m. on Friday (2300 GMT Thursday).</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
